  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amin Ansari vs The State Of Jharkhand ..... Opposite ... on 27 February, 2018 Author: Ananda Sen Bench: Ananda Sen In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi B.A. No. 1041 of 2018 Amin Ansari ..... Petitioner -V e r s u s- The State of Jharkhand ..... Opposite Party ..... Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Ananda Sen ..... For the Petitioner : Mr. Nehala Sharmin, Advocate For the State : A.P.P ..... 2/27.02.2018",
    "facts": "The petitioner is an accused for allegedly committing offence punishable under Sections 429, 406, 188, 120-B/34 of the Indian Penal Code, Sections 11(a)(d)(e)(i)(k) of Prevention of Cruelty to Animals Act, 1960, Rule 3 of the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals (Slaughter House) Rule, 2001, Section 55 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. It is alleged that some camels were confiscated before Bakrid, and were seized and entrusted to the petitioner. The petitioner could not produce the said camels when there were directed to produce. It is alleged that the petitioner had slaughtered the said animals.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that he has falsely been implicated in this case. He submits that the petitioner is in custody since 16.01.2017.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that he has falsely been implicated in this case. He submits that the petitioner is in custody since 16.01.2017.",
